Rationale (brief):
Analyzer shows the population moved toward larger cliff_margin (mean 0.1282 ↑ from 0.0904) while robust_performance_mc fell (mean 0.4453 ↓ from 0.4675) and its estimator noise roughly doubled (std 0.0690 vs 0.0327). That pattern is consistent with objective-weighting pushing the search too conservatively: cliff_margin (1.2) is pulling candidates away from the failure boundary at the expense of the true goal (expected/robust performance). Also nominal_performance (0.5) appears to conflict with the robust objective. A modest rebalancing to emphasize robust_performance_mc and reduce cliff_margin and nominal_performance should steer search back toward designs that improve expected performance under tolerance.

